From: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Feb 2024 17:46:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: run the DFS CAC after the CSA countdown

cfg80211 rejects a CSA to a DFS channel that still needs a CAC. An AP
that must leave a radar channel therefore cannot move to such a
channel with a CSA.

mac80211 now completes the countdown, runs the CAC on the new channel
and finalizes the switch when the CAC ends. Beaconing stays off during
the CAC, so that a later CSA does not reuse a stale CSA beacon. A
radar during the CAC cancels it, allows a new CSA and tells the driver
to end a quiet that it applied for the switch. A background chain that
overlaps the new channel stops when the CAC starts. If a radar hit the
new channel during the countdown, the AP stops instead, because a CAC
would end the non-occupancy period early. The channel that the AP
leaves keeps the two second grace before it expires.

Signed-off-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Co-developed-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
